  [1m[38;5;63m+[0m  read 4x more lines        [1m[38;5;63mA[0m  read the whole log, the older files the kubelet rotated too (KDASH_LOG_MAX_BYTES)
     older files are on the node: read with get nodes/proxy when your RBAC allows it (KDASH_NODE_LOGS=0: never)
     the rule shows what was read and since when: "newest only", "current file", "whole log: 3 rotated files + the current file"

 [1m[38;5;63mS[0m  shell in the container    [1m[38;5;63mU[0m  upload a file             [1m[38;5;63mD[0m  download a file
 S/U/D need --allow-interactive: they run in your name and are audited writes.
 / keeps the context around every match and highlights it; & hides everything else.
 A search covers the whole log: / reads all of it first (the rotated files too, with get nodes/proxy), so the count covers every line.
 F searches the logs of every container of this pod, its workload or the namespace (and the
 previous instance of restarted containers); matches of all logs are merged in time order.
 Prompts: Up / Down recall earlier entries, Left / Right / Home / End edit, Esc cancels.
 A lowercase pattern ignores case: /error finds ERROR and error.
 n and N wrap around and put the match at the top of the pane.
 c lists every container with readiness, restarts, state and last exit: pick one
 and l/p read that container. Search and level stay active across panes.
 w writes the filtered pane to /workspace/kdash/artifacts/live-e2e-v4390/reports/inspector/ (review it before sharing).

 any key returns

















